hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2957","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr, informed us Ibn Jurayj, who narrated to me 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA) that the Prophet (ﷺ) granted permission to al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib (RA) when he sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to stay in Makkah during the nights of Mina for the sake of providing water (Siqayah). So, the Prophet (ﷺ) permitted him.\n\nCHAPTER:"
